  "aboutSaganaDeveloperLabel": "Developer",
  "aboutCooperative": "About the Cooperative",
  "aboutCooperativeBody": "SP3 Agriculture Cooperative (Samahan ng Pagkakaisa sa Pag-unlad ng Payanas) serves farmer-members in Barangay Payanas, Torrijos, Marinduque. It was officially registered with the Cooperative Development Authority (CDA) on February 1, 2017 (Registration No. 9520-1040000000036899), and is classified as a Micro cooperative.\n\nMembers share in the cooperative's income through two mechanisms recognized in its by-laws: Balik-Tangkilik (a patronage refund based on how much of their produce a member sells to the cooperative) and Interest on Share Capital (based on each member's accumulated capital-share contributions). The cooperative's main lines of business include Copra Buy and Sell, Peanut Cookies Production, and Rice and Feeds Retailing, and its members primarily grow peanut, ginger, banana, and palay (rice).\n\nTo become a member, a resident of Barangay Payanas must be at least 18 years old and contribute a minimum of ₱100 a month toward capital build-up, along with an annual capital share of ₱2,000.\n\nEmail Address\n(placeholder — to be provided)\n\nContact Number\n(placeholder — to be provided)",
  "privacyPolicy": "Privacy Policy",
  "privacyPolicyBody": "This Privacy Policy explains what personal information SAGANA collects, why, and how it is used, based on how the system is actually built today.\n\nWhat we collect: your full name, phone number, and profile photo, common to all accounts. Farmer accounts also collect date of birth, gender, farm details, and crop information. Buyer accounts may additionally collect date of birth, gender, and a real contact email. Manager and Officer accounts collect position and department information.\n\nHow you sign in: Farmer, Officer, and Manager accounts sign in with a cooperative-assigned username rather than a public email address — SAGANA uses this internally to create your account, but it is never shown to other users. Buyer accounts may register with a real email address.\n\nWhy we collect it: to operate your cooperative membership (including capital-share and Balik-Tangkilik records), to issue and track agricultural loans, to run the marketplace (listings, orders, and Ginger market-linking with DA-AMAD), and to contact you about cooperative matters such as BOD meetings and loan reminders.\n\nHow it's stored and protected: your information is stored in a managed Supabase database with row-level security rules that restrict each account to its own records. Manager and Officer accounts have broader access strictly for the cooperative operations described above — for example, to review a loan application or approve a marketplace listing — not for unrelated purposes.\n\nWho can see your information: other Farmers and Buyers do not see your personal contact details directly; they only see what's needed for a specific transaction, such as a marketplace listing's crop and price. Manager and Officer accounts can see Farmer and Buyer information needed for cooperative operations, including your farm location and crops, which are used for the Supply Chain map.\n\nUpdating your information: you can update your own name, phone number, photo, gender, and date of birth (where applicable) at any time from Edit Profile. Your username and login email cannot be changed after registration.\n\nAccount suspension: an Manager may suspend an account for cause, with a reason recorded. Suspension blocks login but does not automatically delete your records — SAGANA does not currently have a self-service account or data deletion feature; if you need your data removed, please contact the cooperative directly using the information in About the Cooperative.\n\nSecurity: passwords are managed through Supabase's authentication service and are never visible to cooperative staff. An Manager can issue you a one-time temporary password if you lose access to your account.\n\nQuestions: for privacy concerns, please reach out to the cooperative using the contact information in About the Cooperative.",
  "termsOfUse": "Terms of Use",
  "termsOfUseBody": "By using SAGANA, you agree to the following terms, based on how the system actually works today.\n\nAccounts and roles: SAGANA has four roles — Manager, Officer, Farmer, and Buyer. Manager and Officer accounts are created by the cooperative; Officers can use every Manager feature except managing cooperative membership. Farmer accounts may be created by the Manager or through self-registration followed by Manager review and approval. Buyer accounts may self-register.\n\nAccurate information: you agree to provide accurate, truthful information — including harvest records, crop listings, and personal details — and to keep it up to date through Edit Profile.\n\nMarketplace: Farmer listings require Manager or Officer approval before they appear to Buyers. Ginger harvests may also be sold through DA-AMAD Market Linking or offered directly to the cooperative (Offer to Cooperative) as alternatives to a public listing. Buyers and Farmers are both responsible for honoring the terms of any order they place or accept.\n\nLoans: loans issued through SAGANA are agricultural input loans (such as fertilizer, feeds, or seeds), not cash, and are only available to members meeting the cooperative's capital-share eligibility requirement. Repayment schedules follow the terms shown at the time the loan is issued.\n\nBalik-Tangkilik and capital share: any Balik-Tangkilik or Interest on Share Capital figures shown in SAGANA are estimates based on recorded activity during the year; actual distributions are determined and approved at the cooperative's Annual General Assembly, not by the app.\n\nAccount security: you are responsible for keeping your login credentials confidential and must not share your account with another person. If you suspect unauthorized access, contact the cooperative immediately.\n\nSuspension: the Manager may suspend an account for cause — such as fraudulent information, misuse of the marketplace, or violation of these terms — with a reason recorded. A suspended account cannot log in until reactivated.\n\nOffline use: some features work offline and sync automatically once a connection is available. Actions recorded offline (such as a harvest entry) may not be visible to others until that sync completes.\n\nSystem availability: SAGANA is a cooperative-internal system built as a capstone project, not a commercial platform, and availability is not guaranteed at all times.\n\nChanges to these terms: these terms may be updated as SAGANA's features change. Continued use of SAGANA after an update constitutes acceptance of the revised terms.",
